"'''See You Again'''" is a song by American rapper [[Wiz Khalifa]] featuring American singer-songwriter [[Charlie Puth]]. Produced by Puth, [[DJ Frank E]] and Andrew Cedar, who also co-wrote the song with Khalifa, the song was commissioned for the [[Furious 7 (soundtrack)|soundtrack]] of the 2015 film ''[[Furious 7]]'' as a tribute to ''[[Fast & Furious]]'' actor [[Paul Walker]], who died in a [[single-vehicle crash]] on November 30, 2013. The song was released on March 10, 2015, before ''Furious 7'' was released, as the soundtrack's lead single. It was later included as a bonus track on the international release of Puth's debut album, ''[[Nine Track Mind]]'' (2016).

"See You Again" became both artists' biggest single to date. It spent 12 non-consecutive weeks atop the US [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]], tying with [[Eminem]]'s "[[Lose Yourself]]" for the second longest-running rap number-one single in the country behind [[Lil Nas X]]'s "[[Old Town Road]]", and topped the [[UK Singles Chart]] for two consecutive weeks.<ref>{{cite magazine|title=Wiz Khalifa's 'See You Again' Leads Hot 100 for 10th Week|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/wiz-khalifa-see-you-again-hot-100-10th-week/|access-date=June 30, 2015}}</ref> It also reached number one in several other countries including Australia, Austria, Canada, Germany, Ireland, New Zealand and Switzerland. The song held the record for the most-streamed track in a single day on [[Spotify]] in the United States, until it was surpassed by [[One Direction]]'s "[[Drag Me Down]]".<ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/ed-sheeran-new-spotify-record-24-hour-streams/|title=Ed Sheeran Blasts to New Spotify Record for One-Day Streams|magazine=Billboard|access-date=November 29, 2017}}</ref> It set the record for most streams in a single week worldwide, and in the United Kingdom also in a single week.

The music video was the [[list of most-viewed YouTube videos#Historical most-viewed videos|most-viewed video on YouTube]] from July 10 to August 4, 2017. "See You Again" received three nominations at the [[58th Annual Grammy Awards]]: [[Grammy Award for Song of the Year|Song of the Year]], [[Grammy Award for Best Pop Duo/Group Performance|Best Pop Duo/Group Performance]] and [[Grammy Award for Best Song Written for Visual Media|Best Song Written for Visual Media]]. It was also shortlisted for the Song of the Year for the [[BBC Music Awards]] and was nominated for [[Golden Globe Award for Best Original Song|Best Original Song]] at the [[73rd Golden Globe Awards]].<ref>{{cite news|last1=Merry|first1=Stephanie|last2=Yahr|first2=Emily|title=Golden Globes nominations 2016: Complete list|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/arts-and-entertainment/wp/2015/12/10/golden-globes-nominations-2016-complete-coverage/|access-date=December 10, 2015|newspaper=[[The Washington Post]]|date=December 10, 2015}}</ref> "See You Again" was the best selling-song of 2015 worldwide, with combined sales and track-equivalent streams of 20.9 million units according to [[International Federation of the Phonographic Industry|IFPI]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.ifpi.org/downloads/GMR2016.pdf|title=IFPI Global Music Report|publisher=[[International Federation of the Phonographic Industry|IFPI]]|date=April 12, 2016|access-date=April 12, 2016|archive-date=July 30, 2016|archive-url=https://archive.today/20160730180434/http://www.ifpi.org/downloads/GMR2016.pdf|url-status=dead}}</ref> It is certified Diamond by the [[Recording Industry Association of America]] (RIAA),<ref>{{Cite web|last=McIntyre|first=Hugh|url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/hughmcintyre/2018/11/21/wiz-khalifa-and-charlie-puths-see-you-again-has-been-certified-diamond/|title=Wiz Khalifa And Charlie Puth's 'See You Again' Has Been Certified Diamond|magazine=Forbes|date=November 21, 2018|access-date=September 17, 2023}}</ref> and is one of the [[List of Spotify streaming records|most-streamed songs on Spotify ever]], with over 2.5 billion streams.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://open.spotify.com/track/2JzZzZUQj3Qff7wapcbKjc|title=Wiz Khalifa - See You Again (feat. Charlie Puth)|publisher=Spotify|access-date=August 30, 2026}}</ref>

